*.bak
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
# A Windows agent can leave a real NTFS device-name entry behind when a
# redirect meant for another shell is interpreted literally. It is never
# project content, and Git must not offer it to `git add -A`.
/nul
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.freebuff/
# The tree is `*` rather than the bare directory: git cannot re-include a file
# whose parent directory is excluded, so the one subdirectory that MUST ship
# would be unreachable by a negation.
.saipen/recovery/*
# ...except the compacted LOG detail bodies. A tracked LOG line reading
# `detail_ref: .saipen/recovery/log-detail/...` delegates its own evidence
# there, and `verification_evidence` classifies on that resolved text. With
# the directory excluded, every clone re-read those lines as a bare pointer:
# 11 DONE closures on this repository read unproven the moment anyone else
# cloned it, and the canonical validator went red on a clean checkout while
# green in the maintainer's tree. Half a megabyte makes the shipped LOG read
# the same everywhere it is read.
!.saipen/recovery/log-detail/
# ...and the closed BOARD rows a CLEAN scrub pruned (T-1640). The scrub's DEC
# names the copy and its sha256, and a row closed since the last commit has no
# other durable home once it leaves BOARD.md: with the directory excluded it
# would exist on one machine only, and "moved, never dropped" would be false.
!.saipen/recovery/board-scrub/
# ...and the full records of compacted BOARD rows (T-1668). A row over the
# live cap keeps a compact projection and cites its record by detail_ref;
# with the store excluded a clone read 101 live rows with their text gone
# and nothing reported it. The compaction's lineage checkpoints and the LOG
# tails a repair cut away are cited by tracked lines the same way.
!.saipen/recovery/board-compaction/
!.saipen/recovery/board-compaction-lineage/
!.saipen/recovery/log-foreign-tail/
!.saipen/recovery/log-normalize/
# Durable stores this repository does not ship, one line each with its
# reason; tools/test_t1668_durable_stores_ship.py fails on any other.
# unshipped-durable: .saipen/recovery/settled/ -- the per-operation journal (110 MB, 10984 records on 2026-10-08); a checkout without it reads as no ledger here (journal.resolvable_op_ids), never as forged history
# unshipped-durable: .saipen/recovery/conformance/ -- per-machine validation receipts (23 MB); a clone validates for itself and inherits no verdict
.saipen/locks/
# Exact quarantined receipt bodies are local source authority, never a Git or
# archive distribution surface. Export-safe state stays under intake/distribution.
.saipen/quarantine/
# T-994: process-local runtime caches must never enter the tree.
.saipen/cache/
# bootstrap/export.* drops its archive in the project root by design
saipen_export_*.tar.gz
saipen_export_*.zip

thoughts/

# Project scratch directory for ad-hoc debugging artifacts. It is not shipped
# documentation or source; the validator's coverage stage and the audit checks
# must never classify a file under it as a released Markdown document.
/_tmp_dbg/

# A subSaipen's kitchen is a sandbox, and saiwiki's holds a CLONE of the
# GitHub wiki -- a nested git repository. `git add -A` turns that into a
# gitlink: a 160000 entry pointing at a commit no clone of this repo can
# fetch, with none of the content. It landed in v7.122.0 exactly that way.
.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/wiki/

# T-1350: the same rule, one directory over. saipython's `pen/` is the other
# kitchen sandbox -- its own tracked marker says "Clones of target files land
# here (read from the main tree, edited only as copies). Never the originals.
# Scratch" -- and it was missed when the wiki case was ruled on. It had grown
# two nested git repositories and 1534 untracked scratch files, including whole
# copies of this repository's tools/saipen.py and tools/saipen_engine/, all of
# which the whole-project delivery inventory was collecting as real content.
# The marker itself stays tracked, so the directory keeps saying what it is.
.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/pen/*
!.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/pen/_gitkeep

# Per-machine agent permissions. Untracked and unshared on purpose: it is
# local trust, not project content, and `git add -A` would otherwise publish
# one machine's allowlist as everyone's.
.claude/settings.local.json
.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/_gen_*.py
saipen-delivery.zip

# Wave 15 handoff artifact: large roadmap file, not shipped runtime. Keep out of
# root-file-set and coverage checks; validator honours .gitignore.
impl1.md

# Installed launcher bytes are RENDERED at install time from the single source
# owner bootstrap/cli_launcher.py, into <skill>/bin/. The repository copy would
# only ever name the maintainer clone (absolute interpreter + checkout path), so
# it is a generated artifact, never a tracked one.
/bin/

# The top-level research kitchen. Its scratch held 4547 files / 90 MB: per-ticket
# run logs, one-shot probe and mutation-candidate scripts, live-agent
# stdout/stderr, and five whole-repo candidate trees. None of it is protocol,
# runtime, or evidence -- it is what a ticket's build step happened to write --
# and a fresh `git clone` was paying 90 MB to receive it. The CI TEST TREE CLEAN
# gate already declared untracked `.saipen/kitchen/` debris a failure; tracking
# it was the only reason that gate never fired.
#
# The two registry files are project memory and stay tracked, so the directory
# keeps saying what it is.
/.saipen/kitchen/*
!/.saipen/kitchen/cohort_registry.json
!/.saipen/kitchen/digest.md
# ...and the release receipts (T-1668). closure._published_releases reads
# them as the publication evidence a fresh clone can see; ignored, a clone
# could not resolve one inherited_verified closure and validate --gate core
# failed there while green here.
!/.saipen/kitchen/release_receipt.json
!/.saipen/kitchen/release_receipts/

# saitranslate is a subSaipen, so its kitchen is a sandbox under the same rule
# as `.saipen/extensions/subs/*/kitchen/` above, and its `.translation-cache` is
# a process-local cache under the same rule as `.saipen/cache/` (T-994). Both
# shipped anyway: 2093 files, 20 MB, none of it a translated locale anyone reads
# from the repository. `.prepare-staging/` is the loader's scratch. SUPERSEDED/
# holds packages that lost their race and can never be published.
#
# READY/ and SETTLED/ stay tracked: those are packages still owed a publish.
/.saipen/saitranslate/kitchen/
/.saipen/saitranslate/.translation-cache/
/.saipen/saitranslate/.prepare-staging/
/.saipen/saitranslate/SUPERSEDED/

# tool-module-identity is a tool-comparison scratchpad: a copied-out subject
# repo plus the candidate modules and green/red transcripts a build step wrote
# next to them. Not protocol, not evidence -- 3809 untracked files, and the
# nested subject tree carries paths past what `git add -A` will index on Windows.
# That is not merely untidy: `tools/audit_checks.py` opens its mutation sweep
# with `git add -A`, so on such a checkout the very first probe died on git's
# error and the 247-control sweep never ran.
/.saipen/evidence/tool-module-identity/

# scenario/unit run transcripts written at the repository root by the runner
# harnesses (`scen1612.log`, `unit1612.log`). Scratch, never evidence: they are
# not read by any tool, and validate.py [root-file-set] FAILs on any root file the
# closed set does not name. Its own message names .gitignore as the place a
# scratch file belongs, which is what this is.
scen*.log
unit*.log

# `provable` is a 20-byte scratch marker a host hook wrote at the repository
# root (content: one `code: CHECKPOINTED` line, no consumer in any tool or
# document). validate.py [root-file-set] names .gitignore as the home for
# scratch at the root, and git must never offer this to `git add -A`.
/provable

# A phase transition whose stdout was redirected into a file named after the
# phase (`saipen transition BUILD > BUILD`) leaves an 83-byte status receipt at
# the repository root: `ticket:/phase:/next_action:/code: TRANSITIONED` and
# nothing else. Three arrived that way (BUILD, forensic, prove) from earlier
# sessions. validate.py [root-file-set] names .gitignore as the home for root
# scratch, and git must never offer these to `git add -A`.
/BUILD
/forensic
/prove

# Local third-party tool configuration: `.cbmignore` scopes the code-graph
# indexer and `.mcp.json` registers its MCP server. Both are machine-local
# paths (`C:\Users\...\codebase-memory-mcp.exe`), so they are configuration a
# checkout must own for itself, never project content to publish.
/.cbmignore
/.mcp.json
